This repository contains no Olympus / OM Digital Solutions firmware. The builder downloads the
official firmware from OM's own server on the user's machine.

Third-party:
- external/oly_fw_analysis (git submodule, fishcu, pinned at a61498e): PEN-F firmware research, the container
  format tools and the MN103 emulator harness, used by the developer build and verification tools only. It is not
  part of Caduceus and keeps its own licences: its original contributions are Apache-2.0 (since a61498e), with the
  exceptions it documents in its RIGHTS-AND-PROVENANCE.md (GPL-3.0 for the GNU simulator integration, font-derived
  artwork, third-party material). It is not needed to build or install Caduceus.
- webapp/src/om3.ts, webapp/src/om3names.ts, webapp/src/split.ts, webapp/src/om3films.ts, webapp/src/data/om3films.json
  (its film sims, androidfanman's own designs) and webapp/tests/om3.test.ts are from Caduceus for OM-3
  (androidfanman/caduceus-om3 @ c209b69, its v0.29.5, Apache-2.0, Copyright 2026 androidfanman), unchanged, with a
  source line added to each .ts file (the test file also has our library path and three cases skipped). The OM-3 WB
  mode list, Kelvin range and film-WB parser in webapp/src/pack.ts (WB_MODES, KELVIN, parseFilmWb) are from its
  webapp/src/pack.ts at the same commit. webapp/tests/om3-v0.29.5-looks.ts holds its releases/v0.29.5/LOOKS.BIN
  (its 20 film sims) as base64, as a test fixture.
- The colour-grain method (CPU grain on the developed photo through the bus window) follows Caduceus for OM-3
  (androidfanman/caduceus-om3, Apache-2.0), research/grain/model.py and firmware/src/xblock.s. The E-P7 code in
  patches/grain_cpu is our own.
- The Control Panel preview's before / after divider (the original on a clipped canvas over the look, a draggable
  line set by a --cut variable) follows the design of the Look Lab panel in Caduceus for OM-3 (androidfanman/caduceus-om3,
  Apache-2.0). The code in webapp/src/main.ts and webapp/src/style.css is our own.
- webapp/public/fonts/om3label.woff2: a renamed ASCII subset of DejaVu Sans Condensed (Bitstream Vera
  licence; DejaVu changes public domain), see webapp/public/fonts/FONT-LICENSE.txt.
- 65:24 aspect fixes adapted from flickering-star's work (fork of oly_fw_analysis), with thanks.
  patches/aspect_fix (issue #23) uses that fork's site list and approach (branch ep7-aperture-ar, GPL-3.0);
  the stubs and data there are written for our ids 6/7, see docs/ASPECT.md section 1i.
- patches/mdial (the M-mode dial for manual lenses) is ported from phocean/omsystem-ep7 (Apache-2.0, Copyright 2026
  phocean): its patches/dial_iso and patches/dial_expcomp, with the same bytes; only the stub's address changes.
- Community film recipes are credited to their authors in docs/LIBRARY_V1.md.

